Register `cancel_epic_tasks` in `src/mcp/tools/lifecycle.ts` alongside `cancel_task`, `inputSchema: { project_id, epic_id, reason?, force? }`. Since partial success (some skipped) is the normal case here, not an exceptional one, return `jsonResult({ ok: true, ...result })` even when `skipped` is non-empty — don't use `conflictResult`/`isError` for that, reserve uncaught errors (unknown project/epic) for the framework's default handling, same as the other lifecycle tools.

